Internal email: Opinions on the handling of {ticket} applications (handled by: Social Security Relations Section)
{date}
This document is for the transfer and continuation of cross-province relationships for insured individuals. The list of materials consists of five items: ID card, proof of insurance payment, transfer and continuation application form, labor contract, and contact letter from the receiving location. After signing for each item, 4 items were actually received, but the labor contract was not provided for any item, and 1 item was missing. According to current standards, missing item ≥1 means incomplete materials, and missing items are considered complete if there is zero. This case should be notified in advance. Regarding branching, for matters involving social security enrollment, benefit claims, or relationship transfers, only the social security enrollment, benefit application, and relationship transfer window can be transferred; transfers to other windows are not allowed. Urgency has four levels: if the transfer is delayed and will affect the payment of benefits, it is called urgent; if it is committed to be completed within 3 working days, it is expedited; if completed within the usual 10 working days, it is recorded as standard; if there is no time limit, it is recorded as routine; There are 20 working days left before the validity period of the certificate at the place of transfer expires. Processed according to the usual time limit and recorded as standard. Also: The file scanning task for the {batch} batch is scheduled until next week and is unrelated to this case.
